This directory contains a simple use case of multi criterion optimization.
A user-defined number of parabolas with adjustable location of their minimum represent 
possibly opposing evaluation criteria. Geneva's EA implementation of pareto-front 
optimization is used to tackle this problem. Make sure that the parameter "sortingMode"
is set to 3 or 4 in config/GEvolutionaryAlgorithm.json (this is the default in 
the configuration file provided with this example).

The example has no main() of its own: it is a runtime-loadable module,
libGMultiCriterionParabolaIndividual.so, that the generic optimizer of example 18 loads:

  GGenericOptimizer --individual ./libGMultiCriterionParabolaIndividual.so

GMultiCriterionParabolaIndividual.{hpp,cpp} hold the individual (its criteria and their
evaluation); GMultiCriterionParabolaIndividualPlugin.cpp is only the module's entry point
(gem_module_manifest(), which names the individual's factory and its configuration file).

